Okay.  But in fact "ga'i" means that the speaker is of higher rank than
the referent, just as ".ui" means that the speaker feels happy about the
referent.  So "ga'i" is indeed hauteur.  I like the suggestion of
"abasement" for "ga'inai".

> Dare I say it?  I don't see ci'a - cnita (below) assigned in the
